      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-13T14:40:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, that\u0027s allowed. See next_arg in the kernel source code.\n\nhttps://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/latest/source/lib/cmdline.c#L238\n```\n\tfor (i \u003d 0; args[i]; i++) {\n\t\tif (isspace(args[i]) \u0026\u0026 !in_quote)\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\tif (equals \u003d\u003d 0) {\n\t\t\tif (args[i] \u003d\u003d \u0027\u003d\u0027)\n\t\t\t\tequals \u003d i;\n\t\t}\n\t\tif (args[i] \u003d\u003d \u0027\"\u0027)\n\t\t\tin_quote \u003d !in_quote;\n\t}\n```\n\n* the loop ends on when it sees a space that is not inside a quote pair.\n* inside the loop, in_quote can be turned on and off many times.\n\nI *think* this is to accept a pattern like `foo\u003dvalue,\"long value\",value2`",
      "parentUuid": "a219b622_45768376",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 206,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 58
      },
